WEBVTT

NOTE
Betty tries an early version of Earth Jukebox (Zoom, 15 Nov 2026).
Translated from Mandarin with AI assistance (Anthropic Claude), checked against the recording. Kevin and Alvin are on our team.

1
00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:07.800
Kevin (our team): Try the Speak button.
Can you press it?

2
00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:10.200
Betty (in English): I was born in Sibu.

3
00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:14.000
Kevin: Now find the one next to it:
“Add this place to my tune”.

4
00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:17.120
Betty: OK, I found it.

5
00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:20.240
Betty: Oh… now I can hear it. OK.

6
00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:23.000
Kevin: Do you hear a piece of music?

7
00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:27.500
Betty: Yes. It goes up and down,
like a ringtone.

8
00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:29.840
Kevin: Yes, yes, exactly.

9
00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:33.560
Alvin (our team): I mean, can you use it,
like this?

10
00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:40.200
Betty: Mm. Like this, yes, I can use it.
This way it works.

11
00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:46.120
Betty: It's just that at the start,
I didn't know what each button was for.

12
00:00:46.150 --> 00:00:52.920
Betty (later): You don't know how to work it,
so it's a bit… hard to handle.

13
00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:58.200
Betty: But if you use it every day,
once you understand it, it's easy.
